# =============================================================================
# BIRANCHI KULESIKA — LOCAL DEVELOPMENT ENVIRONMENT CONFIGURATION (.env.example)
# =============================================================================
# Copy this file to `.env.local` for local development:
#   cp .env.example .env.local
#
# The application uses Supabase PostgreSQL for all dynamic data storage and media.
# Must-have variables are active below with development defaults or placeholders.
# Feature-specific variables (Razorpay, Pexels, AI) that are optional for local
# development are provided as commented entries with full documentation.
# =============================================================================


# =============================================================================
# 1. CORE APPLICATION & DOMAIN (MANDATORY)
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Variable name: NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL
# 2. What it is: The canonical public base URL of the website.
# 3. Why the app needs it: Required for generating canonical SEO tags, sitemap.xml,
#    robots.txt, dynamic Open Graph images, JSON-LD structured schemas, and OAuth callbacks.
# 4. Where to get it: Set to http://localhost:3000 for local development.
# 5. Expected format: Full URL without trailing slash (e.g., http://localhost:3000).
# 6. Used by:
#    - lib/config/env.ts -> getSiteUrl(), getSiteDomain()
#    - lib/constants.ts -> SITE_URL, SITE_DOMAIN
#    - lib/seo.ts -> rootMetadata, postMetadata, noteMetadata, websiteJsonLd
#    - app/sitemap.ts -> dynamic sitemap entries
#    - app/robots.ts -> sitemap link
#    - app/admin/login/actions.ts -> OAuth redirect URL
# 7. Server/client: Client-safe (prefixed with NEXT_PUBLIC_).
# 8. Security implications: Public identifier.
# 9. Common mistakes: Adding a trailing slash (e.g., http://localhost:3000/), which
#    causes double slashes in generated links.
# 10. Troubleshooting: If Open Graph images or sitemaps show incorrect domains,
#     verify that NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL matches your active local port.
# 11. Required: Yes (Must have).
# 12. Environment behavior: http://localhost:3000 in dev; https://yourdomain.com in prod.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000


# =============================================================================
# 2. SUPABASE (POSTGRESQL DATABASE, AUTH & STORAGE) (MANDATORY)
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SUPABASE_URL
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Variable name: SUPABASE_URL
# 2. What it is: The HTTPS API gateway URL of your Supabase project.
# 3. Why the app needs it: Connects the application to Supabase for database queries,
#    user authentication, role checks, and asset storage.
# 4. Where to get it:
#    Supabase Dashboard (https://supabase.com/dashboard)
#    → Select your project
#    → Project Settings (Gear icon in sidebar)
#    → API
#    → Project URL
# 5. Expected format: https://<project-ref>.supabase.co
# 6. Used by:
#    - lib/config/env.ts -> getSupabaseUrl()
#    - lib/supabase/server.ts -> getSupabaseAdmin(), getSupabasePublic(), getSupabaseServer()
#    - lib/supabase/client.ts -> getSupabaseBrowser()
#    - app/admin/login/actions.ts
#    - app/admin/auth/callback/route.ts
# 7. Server/client: Client-safe (automatically resolved by lib/config/env.ts).
# 8. Security implications: Public API endpoint. Table data is protected by Row-Level Security (RLS).
# 9. Common mistakes: Copying the postgresql:// direct connection string instead of the HTTPS URL.
# 10. Troubleshooting: If database connection fails with network errors, verify the project
#     URL is active and not paused in the Supabase dashboard.
# 11. Required: Yes (Must have).
# 12. Environment behavior: Points to your local/development or shared Supabase project.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
SUPABASE_URL=https://xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx.supabase.co

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Variable name: NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY
# 2. What it is: The Supabase anonymous/publishable API key.
# 3. Why the app needs it: Authorizes browser and server operations governed by
#    Row-Level Security (RLS) policies (public reads, user login, passkey ceremonies).
# 4. Where to get it:
#    Supabase Dashboard
#    → Project Settings
#    → API
#    → Project API keys
#    → anon / public
# 5. Expected format: Long JWT string (eyJhbGciOi...) or modern key format (sb_pub_...).
# 6. Used by:
#    - lib/config/env.ts -> getSupabasePublishableKey()
#    - lib/supabase/server.ts -> getSupabasePublic(), getSupabaseServer()
#    - lib/supabase/client.ts -> getSupabaseBrowser()
#    - app/admin/login/actions.ts
#    - app/admin/auth/callback/route.ts
# 7. Server/client: Client-safe (prefixed with NEXT_PUBLIC_).
# 8. Security implications: Safe to expose to browsers. RLS policies control table access.
# 9. Common mistakes: Pasting the service_role secret key here instead of anon.
# 10. Troubleshooting: If public reads fail with 401 Unauthorized, verify that the key
#     belongs to the project configured in SUPABASE_URL.
# 11. Required: Yes (Must have).
# 12. Environment behavior: Matches the development Supabase project.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=eyJhbGciOi...

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Variable name: SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY
# 2. What it is: The Supabase service-role administrative API secret key.
# 3. Why the app needs it: Used by the repository layer (SupabaseContentRepository)
#    to perform administrative CRUD operations, bypassing RLS on trusted server contexts.
# 4. Where to get it:
#    Supabase Dashboard
#    → Project Settings
#    → API
#    → Project API keys
#    → service_role (Secret)
# 5. Expected format: Long JWT string (eyJhbGciOi...) or modern key format (sb_secret_...).
# 6. Used by:
#    - lib/config/env.ts -> getSupabaseSecretKey()
#    - lib/supabase/server.ts -> getSupabaseAdmin()
# 7. Server/client: SERVER-ONLY (CRITICAL SECRET).
# 8. Security implications: CRITICAL. Bypasses all Row-Level Security policies.
#    NEVER prefix with NEXT_PUBLIC_, never commit to Git, never import into client components.
# 9. Common mistakes: Prefixing with NEXT_PUBLIC_ or leaking into client-side code.
# 10. Troubleshooting: If server actions throw "Missing Supabase configuration", verify
#     SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY is present in your .env.local file.
# 11. Required: Yes (Must have).
# 12. Environment behavior: Server-only across all environments.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=eyJhbGciOi...


# =============================================================================
# 3. RAZORPAY (PATRONAGE & SUPPORT PAYMENTS) (OPTIONAL FOR LOCAL DEV)
# =============================================================================
# Optional for local development. When unset, the support page (/support) uses an
# instant simulated payment confirmation flow with receipt generation.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NEXT_PUBLIC_RAZORPAY_KEY_ID
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Variable name: NEXT_PUBLIC_RAZORPAY_KEY_ID
# 2. What it is: Public Razorpay Test Key ID for the client-side checkout modal.
# 3. Why the app needs it: Initializes the Razorpay Checkout popup on /support.
# 4. Where to get it:
#    Razorpay Dashboard (https://dashboard.razorpay.com)
#    → Account & Settings
#    → API Keys
#    → Generate / View Key ID (Test Mode)
# 5. Expected format: rzp_test_xxxxxxxxxxxxxx
# 6. Used by:
#    - components/support-page.tsx -> RazorpayConstructor options
# 7. Server/client: Client-safe (prefixed with NEXT_PUBLIC_).
# 8. Security implications: Public identifier.
# 9. Common mistakes: Pasting the Secret Key instead of Key ID.
# 10. Troubleshooting: If modal shows "Invalid Key ID", verify key matches Test Mode.
# 11. Required: Optional (Commented out until needed).
# 12. Environment behavior: Use rzp_test_... in development; rzp_live_... in production.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NEXT_PUBLIC_RAZORPAY_KEY_ID=rzp_test_...

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Variable name: RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET
# 2. What it is: Private Razorpay API secret key for HMAC signature verification.
# 3. Why the app needs it: Cryptographically verifies payment signatures
#    (HMAC-SHA256 of order_id + payment_id) when confirming patronage.
# 4. Where to get it:
#    Razorpay Dashboard
#    → Account & Settings
#    → API Keys
#    → Key Secret (Test Mode)
# 5. Expected format: 24+ character alphanumeric secret string.
# 6. Used by:
#    - lib/razorpay.ts -> verifyPaymentSignature()
#    - lib/services/content.service.ts -> confirmPayment()
# 7. Server/client: SERVER-ONLY (SECRET).
# 8. Security implications: Secret API key. Keep strictly server-side.
# 9. Common mistakes: Exposing in client-side code or mixing Test and Live keys.
# 10. Troubleshooting: If payment confirmation fails with "Invalid payment signature",
#     ensure RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET matches NEXT_PUBLIC_RAZORPAY_KEY_ID.
# 11. Required: Optional (Commented out until needed).
# 12. Environment behavior: Test secret in dev; Live secret in production.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET=...

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Variable name: RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET
# 2. What it is: Secret token used to verify Razorpay webhook payloads.
# 3. Why the app needs it: Validates the X-Razorpay-Signature header on POST requests
#    to /api/webhooks/razorpay to prevent spoofed payment captured events.
# 4. Where to get it:
#    Razorpay Dashboard
#    → Account & Settings
#    → Webhooks
#    → Add New Webhook (URL: http://localhost:3000/api/webhooks/razorpay via ngrok)
#    → Secret field
# 5. Expected format: Custom secret string chosen during webhook setup.
# 6. Used by:
#    - lib/razorpay.ts -> verifyWebhookSignature()
#    - lib/services/content.service.ts -> processRazorpayWebhook()
#    - app/api/webhooks/razorpay/route.ts
# 7. Server/client: SERVER-ONLY (SECRET).
# 8. Security implications: Secret. Prevents spoofed webhook calls.
# 9. Common mistakes: Putting the API Key Secret instead of the Webhook Secret.
# 10. Troubleshooting: If webhooks return 400 "Invalid webhook signature", verify the secret
#     matches Razorpay Webhook settings.
# 11. Required: Optional (Commented out until needed).
# 12. Environment behavior: Set when using local webhook tunnels (e.g. ngrok).
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET=...


# =============================================================================
# 4. THIRD-PARTY SERVICES & INTEGRATIONS (OPTIONAL FOR LOCAL DEV)
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PEXELS_API_KEY
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Variable name: PEXELS_API_KEY
# 2. What it is: API key for Pexels photo search.
# 3. Why the app needs it: Fetches daily rotating high-resolution atmosphere wallpapers
#    for the admin login screen (/admin/login).
# 4. Where to get it:
#    Pexels API Portal (https://www.pexels.com/api/)
#    → Create free account / Sign in
#    → Your API Key
# 5. Expected format: 56-character alphanumeric string.
# 6. Used by:
#    - lib/services/pexels.service.ts -> fetchFromPexels()
#    - app/api/login-background/route.ts
# 7. Server/client: SERVER-ONLY (SECRET).
# 8. Security implications: Secret API key. Low blast radius (read-only image search).
# 9. Common mistakes: Forgetting to set header Authorization: <key>.
# 10. Troubleshooting: If unset or failing, the login screen seamlessly falls back to
#     curated local dark atmosphere images.
# 11. Required: Optional (Commented out until needed).
# 12. Environment behavior: Safe to share same key across dev and prod.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PEXELS_API_KEY=...

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OPENAI_API_KEY / GROQ_API_KEY / AI_MODEL / OPENAI_BASE_URL
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Variable name: OPENAI_API_KEY or GROQ_API_KEY
# 2. What it is: LLM provider API key for editorial metadata generation.
# 3. Why the app needs it: Automatically generates suggested tags, persona classification,
#    and SEO descriptions in the MDX Composer (/admin/compose).
# 4. Where to get it:
#    OpenAI: https://platform.openai.com/api-keys
#    Groq: https://console.groq.com/keys
# 5. Expected format: sk-proj-... (OpenAI) or gsk_... (Groq).
# 6. Used by:
#    - lib/services/ai-metadata.service.ts -> generateDocumentAiMetadata()
# 7. Server/client: SERVER-ONLY (SECRET).
# 8. Security implications: Secret API key.
# 9. Common mistakes: Exposing in client bundles.
# 10. Troubleshooting: If unset, the composer falls back seamlessly to deterministic
#     local heuristic NLP generation without needing any API key.
# 11. Required: Optional (Commented out until needed).
# 12. Environment behavior: Optional across all environments.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-proj-...
# GROQ_API_KEY=gsk_...
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1/chat/completions
# AI_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID / GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Variable name: GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID / GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET
# 2. What it is: Google OAuth 2.0 credentials for admin login via Google.
# 3. Why the app needs it: Enables Google Sign-In on the admin login page
#    (/admin/login) via Supabase Auth OAuth flow.
# 4. Where to get it:
#    Google Cloud Console (https://console.cloud.google.com)
#    → APIs & Services → Credentials
#    → Create OAuth 2.0 Client ID (Web application type)
# 5. Expected format: Client ID is a alphanumeric string; Client Secret is a
#    short secret string.
# 6. Used by:
#    - supabase/config.toml -> [auth.external.google]
#    - app/admin/login/actions.ts -> signInWithGoogle()
# 7. Server/client: SERVER-ONLY (used by Supabase local config).
# 8. Security implications: Secret credentials. Never expose Client Secret.
# 9. Common mistakes: Using a Desktop or iOS OAuth client type instead of Web.
# 10. Troubleshooting: If Google login fails, verify:
#     - Authorized redirect URI is set to http://127.0.0.1:54321/auth/v1/callback
#     - OAuth consent screen is configured (external or internal)
#     - supabase stop && supabase start after config.toml changes
# 11. Required: Optional (Commented out until needed).
# 12. Environment behavior: Local development only.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
